# Durotar - Completionist (pack butler-routes-completionist, v1).
# The pack's first Horde-block starting-zone route: every Durotar accept in
# the local census (106 quests, docs/durotar-census.md) appears exactly once
# as an accept and once as a turnin. Band 1-13 by minLevel cluster (zone id
# 1411, order 46). Five above-band records, the repeatables, seasonal and
# broken/out-of-zone rest are out with reasons in the census, plus the two
# already-contracted Barrens links (1464/1521) and the Alliance set-asides.
# No race header: Orc, Troll, Tauren and Undead all play this route, with
# per-line gates where the data is exclusive - only Orc,Troll on the Valley
# tablets' Orc halves and the hunter chain, only Hunter,Tauren on 6067, only
# Priest,Troll on the Hex chain's Troll legs and only Priest,Undead on its
# Touch legs, only Shaman,Horde on 98517 (race bit 33, the Horde flag).
# Druid quests gate race-only (only Troll on 3086, only Orc on 98576, only
# Orc,Undead,Troll on 1884) or ungated (1883): the compiler's race/class
# matrix has no Troll/Orc/Undead Druid combos, so class-bearing Druid gates
# error as empty sets - the race half is data-exact and the sim offers per
# the quest data. The Hex/Touch same-name twins (5652/5654, 5660/5662) are
# mutually exclusive in the data: the blocked twin is ordered first (5652 and
# 5662 ride the North leg, 5654 and 5660 follow at the Razor Hill return).
# Soft-pre minis stand alone in dedicated steps: when onquest 787 (Valley
# arrival), when onquest 786 (Kolkar plans), when onquest 1525 (Call of Fire),
# when onquest 97904 (Lau'Tiki's shore run), and the west return for 6082.
# Expedition legs switch frames deliberately and back: Orgrimmar (1454),
# the Barrens (1413), Mulgore (1412), Tirisfal (1420), Sessaria's map (2521).
guide butler-routes-completionist/durotar
title Durotar
levels 1-13
zone Durotar
faction Horde
category Leveling
folder Completionist
coords live
version 1

